# The State ledger is append-only and written from every machine that shares the vault: git
# unions the lines instead of stopping the rebase, and the fold is order-independent (latest
# valid_from wins), so a union is always the right merge for it.
State/facts.jsonl merge=union
State/proposed.jsonl merge=union
# Deliberately NOT Daily/*.md. A union merge of two machines' renders of the same day keeps BOTH
# briefing blocks, silently; a stopped rebase is loud. With the pull step on, the briefing is
# never rendered on a stale tree, so a daily-note conflict should not arise — and if it does, a
# human should see it.
